#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068650 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068807 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "00d1bec1-5f96-5ea9-863e-8f7312c8b526" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Graph of the Cube Root Function"}] :question/id #uuid "efb469e0-ae96-553d-8e7a-56a25739e4af" :question/math-academy-id "e-7942" :question/problem "![](images/06/06a54157969bfc559c8622512bca59b796f8100f8b52542165acb1eb2f397585.png)\n\nWhich of the above could be the graph of $y=\\sqrt[3]{x}$?" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall some of the basic properties of\n\n$$\ny=\\sqrt[3]{x}{:}\n$$\n\n- The point $(0,0)$ lies on the graph.\n- Its domain is $x\\in (-\\infty,\\infty)$.\n- Its range is $y\\in (-\\infty,\\infty)$.\n- The graph lies in the first and third quadrants.\n- The function is increasing throughout its entire domain.\n- As $x \\rightarrow \\infty$, we have $y\\rightarrow \\infty$, though the function increases more slowly as $x$ gets large.\n- As $x \\rightarrow -\\infty$, we have $y\\rightarrow -\\infty$, though the function decreases more slowly as $x$ becomes very negative.\n\nOf the given options, only graph I has all of the above properties. Therefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068651 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068808 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3135b492-14a6-5ccf-9b83-deecba63f7f4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Properties of the Cube Root Function"}] :question/id #uuid "289fd11d-ce6d-5554-a061-9647c67e5326" :question/math-academy-id "e-7943" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $f(x) =\\sqrt[3]{x}$?\n\n1. The point $(64,4)$ lies on the graph of $y=f(x)$\n2. The domain of $f(x)$ is $x\\in[-1,\\infty)$\n3. $f(x) \\rightarrow -\\infty$ as $x \\rightarrow -\\infty$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by recalling the graph of\n\n$$\ny=\\sqrt[3]{x}\n$$\n\n![](images/ab/abafb7d55b4baa0b06f20c3de2b44d5925f7286f078aaa76d71aded7c9c9a001.png)\n\nNow, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, $f(64)=\\sqrt[3]{64}=4$.\n- Statement II is false since $f(x) =\\sqrt[3]{x}$ is defined for $x \\in (-\\infty, \\infty)$.\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, $f(x) \\rightarrow -\\infty$ as $x \\rightarrow -\\infty$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}]}
